  "report": "Packaging reception is positive on appearance and refillability, while failure reports become recurrent in the added evidence. The record supports reported experiences and preferences, not defect prevalence, verified environmental performance or packaging-caused purchasing.\n\nStage comparison: the saved input identifies only an updated stage, without an explicit earlier-stage manifest. Taking the first block (P00–P42 as listed) as initial and the appended P08–P13/R01 as additions, the initial block contains one arrival-leak report (P06), a brand replacement offer (P07), aesthetic/environmental praise, refill requests and buying/loyalty expressions. Its arrival-leak finding is isolated testimony; likes do not supply additional experiences. The additions bring arrival-leak reporting/contextual agreement to seven distinct TikTok profiles in the same reply branch. Only P06 and P13 explicitly describe loose/improperly screwed tops; P08 adds a free replacement reportedly sent, and four replies are bare agreements. This establishes distinct-account recurrence of the broad arrival-leak proposition within one conversation, with unequal detail and unverified human independence. It does not establish seven loose-top diagnoses or seven independently investigated incidents.\n\nR01 separately reports Softwear–Void’s lid repeatedly unscrewing, leakage during pocket carriage at work, clothing stains and unrecoverable product loss. TikTok complaint SKU/version remains unknown; R01 therefore adds retailer-review corroboration for the broader proposition that Experiment packaging leakage is reported across customer source roles, not corroboration of a particular SKU’s arrival defect. Loose closures recur descriptively in P06/P13/R01 under different or unknown product and use conditions; a shared manufacturing cause is unestablished. No supplied evidence isolates a batch, version or joint-use condition.\n\nReception is conditional/mixed: several profiles praise packaging, but those statements do not contradict specific leakage reports. P00’s aesthetic/environmental praise has 296 displayed likes; P15’s proposed reuse has 150. These show endorsement of the statements, not verified recyclability, safe reuse, experiences or buying effects. P03 is the same actor as P00 and offers explicitly uncertain component-recyclability claims; P01 is brand agreement, not independent customer corroboration. P02 questions recyclability. P26 praises packaging while asking what the product does for skin. Refill requests and refillability excitement are distinct from proven environmental benefit.\n\nConsequences remain source-specific. P06 reports opening/cleaning after leakage and worries about oxygen exposure. P07 says short exposure is not an issue and offers a replacement conditional on contacting support; neither safety nor fulfillment is independently verified. P08 says Sephora sent a free replacement, without confirming delivery. R01 remains strongly attached to Void and explicitly intends repurchase despite leakage, lost product and cost frustration; click-lock/doe-foot suggestions are proposed remedies, not implemented fixes. No return, abandonment or completed complaint-driven repurchase is reported. P17 reports an all-Experiment routine and Continuum in transit; P20 expresses buying enthusiasm, P32 tentative saving interest, P38 anticipation of trying, and P42 receipt plus newly discovered refillability. These do not establish packaging as the cause of acquisition or loyalty.\n\nCounts below apply to the full updated focal set and count source-account records as requested, not origins or events. P00/P03 share one actor, as do brand records P01/P07. All TikTok records come from the same brand-video conversation, captured 2026-09-09T11:56:25.935Z; displayed publication dates lack years. All raw focal likes are retained in the index. The supplied capture reports 47 displayed bodies against 72 advertised comments; this is not completeness proof, and other reply branches remain outside the follow-up. Native comment IDs are unavailable. No context-only records were supplied; the video itself cannot supply missing product testimony. R01’s review engagement is unavailable; its rating and recommendation are review metadata, not endorsement counts.",
